  "analysis": "We need to implement the classic Table Compression (Codeforces 650C) solution. The approach is to process the matrix values in increasing order and assign compressed values to cells in groups of equal original value. For each group, cells connected by the same row or column (within that group) form connected components. Each component's compressed value t is 1 plus the maximum of the current row_max[i] and col_max[j] over all rows i and columns j involved in the component (computed using the values assigned for strictly smaller original values). All cells in a component receive the same t, and after processing the whole group, we update row_max and col_max accordingly. This ensures the relative order constraints are preserved and the maximum value is minimized. We implement DSU for components within each group, grouping by row/column to connect cells efficiently, and compute t without influencing other components in the same group until all t's are determined.\n",
